  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 215 PM CDT Mon Oct 5 2026\n\nWednesday night through Monday:\n\nHigh pressure builds in behind the aforementioned cold front,\nwith a light NW breeze and highs in the mid to upper 60s for\nThursday. As this high lingers in the region Thursday night,\nwinds are expected to go light and variable, and if subsidence\nis strong enough / skies are clear enough, we could be looking\nat another threat for patchy frost in susceptible low-lying\nareas. Highs remain in the 60s for Friday with light west or\nsouthwest winds as the high pressure system exits east from the\nregion. \n\nPredictability drops substantially from then onwards, with the\npattern shifting to allow higher amplitude troughs over the\nwestern CONUS and (depending on phasing) some diffluent flow\nover the Plains. Most models leave the weekend predominantly\ndry, followed by higher (15-40%) precip chances into Monday and\nonwards on account of some fast moving low pressure systems /\nbaroclinic zones. \n\nSheppard",
